1
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:05,540
Okay, so we went to the beach because Phoebe found out about this lady...

2
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:06,920
...who knew her mom and dad...

3
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:09,380
...and I don't really know what happened with that.

4
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:11,550
- I'm your mother.     - Huh?

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:14,430
Monica joked that she wouldn't go out with a guy like Chandler.

6
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:16,090
- Hi there.     - He couldn't let it go.

7
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:20,390
I don't really know what happened with that. And then Ross' new girlfriend shows up...

8
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,770
...and Rachel convinced her to shave her head.

9
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:24,560
And then Ross and Rachel kiss.

10
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:27,400
And now Ross has to choose between Rachel and the bald girl.

11
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:30,400
And I don't know what happened there either.

12
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:32,820
You know what? Hold on. Let me go get Chandler.

13
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:46,790
Hi.

14
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,460
- Hi.     - Hey.

15
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:52,710
Rachel was just helping me out. My head got all sunburned.

16
00:00:53,090 --> 00:00:54,470
Aw.

17
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:58,720
- Thanks a million.     - Oh, you're welcome a million.

18
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:01,640
- Okay, I'll be in our room.     - Uh.

19
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:15,530
Oh, my God.

20
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,320
I know.

21
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,870
- Okay, I gotta go.     - Whoa. What? Why?

22
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:26,910
Uh, I gotta go break up with Bonnie.

23
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:29,080
Here? Now?

24
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:31,460
Well, yeah, I can't stay here all night.

25
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:34,710
And if I go in there, she's gonna want to...

26
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:35,920
...do stuff.

27
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:39,760
Can't you just tell here that you are not in the mood?

28
00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:41,430
No, she likes that.

29
00:01:42,510 --> 00:01:44,930
Ha, ha. Yeah, faking sleep doesn't work either.

30
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:47,350
I can't tell you how many mornings I woke up with her...

31
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,020
- Oh.     - Oh, okay.

32
00:01:49,190 --> 00:01:54,270
- Ha, ha. Yeah, why am I telling you?     - I don't know. Ha, ha.

33
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,530
Uh, uh...

34
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,120
- It wasn't every morning...     - Oh, making it worse.

35
00:02:05,290 --> 00:02:06,580
Okay.

36
00:02:57,090 --> 00:02:59,760
So I guess you'd like to know how it all happened.

37
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:02,470
I mean, well, I think I can figure it out.

38
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,930
I guess, you know, I was born...

39
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,470
...and then everyone started lying their asses off.

40
00:03:07,350 --> 00:03:09,770
No, no, it wasn't like that.

41
00:03:09,930 --> 00:03:13,440
I mean, remember how I told you how Lily and Frank and I, we were close?

42
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:16,360
Well, we were very close.

43
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:17,980
How close?

44
00:03:18,150 --> 00:03:21,860
Well, the three of us, we were kind of a, um... A couple.

45
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:26,030
- I don't even know how that would work.     - Well, we...

46
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:27,330
I'm not asking.

47
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:31,910
Well, anyhow, somehow I got pregnant...

48
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,620
...and I was...

49
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:37,590
...scared. I was stupid and selfish and...

50
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:39,500
I was 18 years old.

51
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:42,760
I mean, you remember what it was like to be 18 years old, don't you?

52
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:45,800
Yeah. Let's see, my mom had killed herself and my dad had run off.

53
00:03:45,970 --> 00:03:49,970
And I was living in a gremlin with a guy named Cindy, who talked to his hand.

54
00:03:52,270 --> 00:03:53,690
Oh, I'm so sorry.

55
00:03:53,850 --> 00:03:56,610
I thought I was leaving you with the best parents in the world.

56
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:59,980
I didn't even hear about your mom and dad till a couple of years ago.

57
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:02,070
And by then, you were already grown up.

58
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:04,820
I don't know. You're here and I would really...

59
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:06,870
I would like to get to know you.

60
00:04:07,030 --> 00:04:10,120
Yeah, well, everybody does. Ha, ha.

61
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:12,330
I'm a really cool person.

62
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:14,750
And you know, you had 29 years to find that out...

63
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:16,420
...but you didn't even try.

64
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:20,800
You know what? You walked out on me, and I'm gonna do the same to you.

65
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:24,380
- Wait.     - Okay? I don't ever want to see you again.

66
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:30,100
Where's my purse?

67
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:34,270
Shoot. We're out of soda.

68
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,190
Oh, I'll go out and get you some.

69
00:04:36,350 --> 00:04:39,270
- Really?     - No, because I'm not your boyfriend.

70
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:43,530
Hey, Pheebs, how'd it go?

71
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,610
Huh. Well, ahem...

72
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:49,240
My mom's friend, Phoebe, is actually my birth mom.

73
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:55,000
I found a dried up seahorse.

74
00:04:55,790 --> 00:04:57,370
Sweetie, what are you talking about?

75
00:04:57,540 --> 00:05:00,630
Oh, my new mom, who's a big fat abandoner.

76
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,050
Oh, wait, Pheebs.

77
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:05,380
Wait a second. Don't you want to stay here and talk about it?

78
00:05:05,550 --> 00:05:07,470
No. I just... I wanna...

79
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,640
I need to be alone.

80
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,310
- Monica.     - Oh.

81
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:24,900
It's over.

82
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:30,120
- Oh. Was it awful?     - Well, it was long.

83
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,330
I didn't even realize how late it was...

84
00:05:32,490 --> 00:05:35,040
...till I noticed the five o'clock shadow on her head.

85
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:45,380
Anyway, she didn't want to stay. I called a cab. She just left.

86
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:54,640
I wrote you a letter.

87
00:05:54,810 --> 00:05:57,680
Oh, thank you. Ha, ha.

88
00:05:58,310 --> 00:06:00,230
I like mail.

89
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:06,820
There's just some things I've been thinking about.

90
00:06:06,990 --> 00:06:08,570
You know, things about us.

91
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:11,660
And before we can even think about the two of us getting back together...

92
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:15,370
...I just need to know how you feel about this stuff.

93
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:20,670
- Okay. Heh.     - Okay.

94
00:06:24,170 --> 00:06:25,710
Well, it's...

95
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,050
It's 5:30 in the morning. Heh.

96
00:06:31,050 --> 00:06:35,310
So I'd better get cracking on this baby.

97
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:39,480
So I'll be waiting for you. Just come up when you're done.

98
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,650
Okay. I'll be up...

99
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,900
...in 18 pages.

100
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:48,360
Front and back.

101
00:06:50,150 --> 00:06:52,110
Very exciting.

102
00:07:09,010 --> 00:07:11,220
Oh, oh.

103
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:17,970
Hey.

104
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:20,480
What happened to you? Why didn't you come up?

105
00:07:21,350 --> 00:07:22,690
Done.

106
00:07:24,230 --> 00:07:27,440
- You just finished?     - Well, I wanted to be thorough.

107
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:33,240
I mean, this is clearly very, very important to you. To us.

108
00:07:33,410 --> 00:07:37,240
And so I wanted to read every word carefully.

109
00:07:37,410 --> 00:07:38,450
Twice.

110
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:41,710
So, um...

111
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:44,290
Does it?

112
00:07:50,590 --> 00:07:51,970
I'm sorry?

113
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:59,760
Does it?

114
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:07,810
Yeah, I wanted to give that whole "Does it?" part just another glance.

115
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:11,150
What are you talking about, Ross? You just said that you read it twice.

116
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:14,740
Look, you know what? It either does or doesn't. And if you have to think...

117
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:18,490
No, Rach. No, I don't have to think about it. I don't.

118
00:08:18,660 --> 00:08:19,990
Uh, in fact...

119
00:08:20,580 --> 00:08:23,750
...I've decided. I have decided...

120
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,920
...that it...

121
00:08:31,170 --> 00:08:32,510
...does.

122
00:08:49,270 --> 00:08:52,190
- Are you sure?     - Oh, sure, I'm sure.

123
00:08:58,700 --> 00:09:03,580
All right. There's a nuclear holocaust. I'm the last man on earth.

124
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,120
Would you go out with me?

125
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:09,080
Ehh.

126
00:09:11,630 --> 00:09:12,750
I've got canned goods.

127
00:09:15,130 --> 00:09:17,380
Hey, you guys, take a look at this.

128
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:20,510
Check this baby out. Dug me a hole.

129
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:24,810
Excellent hole, Joe.

130
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,520
Oh, no, no. My hole.

131
00:09:28,690 --> 00:09:30,810
Ow! My foot. Ow!

132
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:32,400
What? What is it?

133
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:36,070
Jellyfish sting. Ow, it hurts, it hurts, it hurts.

134
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:38,280
Well, can we help you, take you back to the house?

135
00:09:38,490 --> 00:09:39,700
Oh, it's, like, two miles.

136
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:42,200
Yeah, and I'm a little tired from digging the hole.

137
00:09:43,870 --> 00:09:45,620
Damn the jellyfish.

138
00:09:45,790 --> 00:09:48,420
Damn all the jellyfish.

139
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:49,710
We've gotta do something.

140
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,420
There's only one thing you can do.

141
00:09:51,590 --> 00:09:52,710
What? What is it?

142
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:54,210
You're gonna have to pee on it.

143
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,050
What? Gross.

144
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,470
Don't blame me. I saw it on the Discovery Channel.

145
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:04,640
You know what? He's right. There's something like ammonia in that...

146
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:06,350
...that kills the pain.

147
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:10,350
Well, forget it. It doesn't hurt that bad!

148
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:13,400
If you want some privacy, you can use my hole.

149
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:20,450
Well, I'm ready to get the hell out of here.

150
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:22,530
Oh.

151
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:23,740
Are you...?

152
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,370
Are you?

153
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:27,410
Oh, that's so great.

154
00:10:27,790 --> 00:10:28,870
Ooh, not for Bonnie.

155
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:32,420
But for you, yay, aah.

156
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,800
How was the beach?

157
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,210
- Nothing. I don't know.     - Uh, let's not worry about it.

158
00:10:40,590 --> 00:10:42,590
- What happened?     - Nothing.

159
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:45,310
- I'm gonna take a shower.     - Me too.

160
00:10:45,470 --> 00:10:47,060
Me too.

161
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:49,730
Okay, I'm gonna put this in the car.

162
00:10:49,890 --> 00:10:52,900
Oh, I have to go pack. Oh!

163
00:10:53,730 --> 00:10:55,980
- And it really does?     - It does.

164
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:58,280
It really and truly does.

165
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,860
Oh.

166
00:11:21,090 --> 00:11:24,510
It so does not.

167
00:11:29,850 --> 00:11:31,940
She wants me to take responsibility...

168
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:35,060
...for everything that went wrong in our relationship.

169
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:40,320
I mean, she goes on for five pages about how I was unfaithful to her.

170
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:43,360
We were on a break!

171
00:11:43,530 --> 00:11:47,660
Oh, my God. If you say that one more time, I'm gonna break up with you.

172
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,490
All right, fine.

173
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:53,040
But this breakup was not all my fault. And she says here:

174
00:11:53,210 --> 00:11:56,710
"If you accept full responsibility..." Full responsibility.

175
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,840
"...I can begin to trust you again.

176
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,510
Does that seem like something you can do? Does it?"

177
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:06,550
No?

178
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:11,180
Look, Ross, you have what you want. You're back with Rachel.

179
00:12:11,350 --> 00:12:14,350
You're gonna wreck the best thing that ever happened to you.

180
00:12:14,730 --> 00:12:17,810
Yeah, I know. I know, you're right.

181
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,440
Yeah, I guess I'll let it go.

182
00:12:20,610 --> 00:12:24,030
But you understand how hard it is to forget about this?

183
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,740
Sure, it's hard to forget...

184
00:12:25,910 --> 00:12:29,120
...but that doesn't mean you have to talk about it.

185
00:12:29,660 --> 00:12:31,330
A lot of things happened on that trip...

186
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:35,500
...that we should never, ever talk about.

187
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,210
What the hell happened on that beach?

188
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:44,880
It's between us and the sea, Ross.

189
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:57,060
- Hi, Ursula.     - Hey.

190
00:12:57,230 --> 00:13:00,320
Okay, well, um, I know that we haven't talked in a long time.

191
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:03,490
But, um, okay, our mom is not our birth mom.

192
00:13:03,650 --> 00:13:05,950
This other lady is our birth mom.

193
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:09,240
Right, okay, the one that lives in Montauk. Mm-hm.

194
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:10,780
You know her?

195
00:13:10,950 --> 00:13:14,790
No. I, um... I read about her in Mom's suicide note.

196
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:17,250
There was a suicide note?

197
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:19,290
Well, do you still have it?

198
00:13:20,290 --> 00:13:21,880
Hang on.

199
00:13:24,050 --> 00:13:27,300
I can't believe you didn't tell me there was a suicide note.

200
00:13:27,470 --> 00:13:29,720
Yeah, so how have you been doing?

201
00:13:29,890 --> 00:13:32,100
I... Shut up.

202
00:13:36,730 --> 00:13:39,440
"Goodbye, Phoebe and Ursula. I'll miss you.

203
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:42,400
P.S: Your mom lives in Montauk."

204
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,780
You just wrote this.

205
00:13:45,990 --> 00:13:48,950
Well, it's pretty much the gist.

206
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:53,330
Except for the poem. You read the poem, right?

207
00:13:53,490 --> 00:13:55,160
No.

208
00:13:55,910 --> 00:13:57,750
All right. Hang on.

209
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:04,880
Pass the cheese, please.

210
00:14:07,170 --> 00:14:08,590
Ugh.

211
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:12,720
My God, you can't even look at me, can you?

212
00:14:12,890 --> 00:14:14,350
No.

213
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:18,140
Yay, it's Phoebe. We can talk to Phoebe.

214
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:22,440
No, I'm too depressed to talk.

215
00:14:22,610 --> 00:14:24,650
I'll give you $1000 to talk to us.

216
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:27,030
Hey, you guys...

217
00:14:27,190 --> 00:14:30,110
...what do you think about making that beach trip an annual thing?

218
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:32,120
No.

219
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:34,700
All right, that's it, you guys. What happened out there?

220
00:14:34,870 --> 00:14:38,250
What? We took a walk. Nothing happened.

221
00:14:38,410 --> 00:14:40,460
I came back with nothing all over me.

222
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:44,130
- Come on, what happened? Joey?     - What does that mean?

223
00:14:45,130 --> 00:14:46,250
- All right.     - No.

224
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:48,460
Joey, we swore we'd never tell.

225
00:14:48,630 --> 00:14:50,800
They'll never understand.

226
00:14:53,970 --> 00:14:55,640
But we have to say something.

227
00:14:55,810 --> 00:14:57,770
We have to get it out. It's eating me alive.

228
00:15:00,690 --> 00:15:04,190
- Monica got stung by a jellyfish.     - All right.

229
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,740
All right.

230
00:15:11,990 --> 00:15:13,870
I got stung.

231
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:16,950
Stung bad.

232
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:20,660
I couldn't stand. I...

233
00:15:20,830 --> 00:15:22,540
I couldn't walk.

234
00:15:22,710 --> 00:15:25,130
We were two miles from the house.

235
00:15:26,670 --> 00:15:28,880
We were scared and alone.

236
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:31,340
We didn't think we could make it.

237
00:15:36,350 --> 00:15:37,850
I was in too much pain.

238
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:40,270
And I was tired from digging the huge hole.

239
00:15:42,810 --> 00:15:45,480
And then Joey remembered something.

240
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,900
I'd seen this thing on the Discovery Channel.

241
00:15:49,070 --> 00:15:50,650
Wait a minute, I saw that.

242
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:55,370
On the Discovery Channel. Yeah, about jellyfish and how if you...

243
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,790
Ew.

244
00:15:59,950 --> 00:16:01,500
You peed on yourself?

245
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,500
Ew.

246
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:07,210
You can't say that. You don't know.

247
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:09,670
I thought I was gonna pass out from the pain.

248
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:13,880
Anyway, I tried, but I couldn't...

249
00:16:14,050 --> 00:16:15,130
...bend that way.

250
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:19,390
So...

251
00:16:20,850 --> 00:16:22,730
Ew.

252
00:16:25,270 --> 00:16:27,900
That's right. I stepped up.

253
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:33,070
She's my friend and she needed help.

254
00:16:33,610 --> 00:16:36,030
If I had to, I'd pee on any one of you.

255
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:44,250
Only, uh, I couldn't.

256
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,840
I got the stage fright.

257
00:16:51,090 --> 00:16:54,090
I wanted to help, but there was just too much pressure...

258
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:56,220
...so I, uh... I turned to Chandler.

259
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:05,440
Joey kept screaming at me, "Do it now. Do it. Do it. Do it now."

260
00:17:06,650 --> 00:17:10,110
Sometimes, late at night, I can still hear the screaming.

261
00:17:13,030 --> 00:17:16,610
That's because, sometimes, I just do it through my wall to freak you out.

262
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:21,950
And fuchsia and mauve

263
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:26,620
Those are the 66 colors of my bedroom

264
00:17:27,670 --> 00:17:29,080
Thank you. Thank you.

265
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:33,880
Oh, and I invite all of you to count the colors in your bedroom.

266
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:37,260
Except for you. You go away.

267
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:43,220
I'll go in a second.

268
00:17:43,390 --> 00:17:45,480
I just want to tell you...

269
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:49,440
...that there hasn't been a day when I didn't regret giving you up.

270
00:17:49,810 --> 00:17:51,770
Okay, bye.

271
00:17:53,150 --> 00:17:54,610
No, I'm not done.

272
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:58,240
I just want you to know, the reason I never looked you up was because...

273
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:00,490
...well, I was afraid that you'd react...

274
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:04,080
...just, well, like the way you're reacting now.

275
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:07,540
Can't we just, you know, start from here? Please?

276
00:18:09,370 --> 00:18:10,670
No.

277
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,420
Okay.

278
00:18:16,170 --> 00:18:17,670
Sorry.

279
00:18:19,970 --> 00:18:21,300
But just one last thing.

280
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:25,180
You know, you came looking for family.

281
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:28,180
I'm family.

282
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,980
I'm it.

283
00:18:33,270 --> 00:18:35,610
Well, now I'm done.

284
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:42,120
Yeah, but it's not like we're losing anything, you know?

285
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:45,330
Yeah, I guess you're right.

286
00:18:45,490 --> 00:18:49,910
It's not like we know each other or anything or that have anything in common.

287
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:55,380
Oh, I don't know. I mean, it's not like we don't have anything in common.

288
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:59,220
I mean, I like, uh, pizza.

289
00:18:59,550 --> 00:19:01,680
I... I like pizza.

290
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:03,590
You do?

291
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:06,180
Wait, I like, um, the Beatles.

292
00:19:06,390 --> 00:19:07,850
Oh, my God. So do I!

293
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:10,060
I knew it. Wow.

294
00:19:10,230 --> 00:19:12,100
Wait, wait, wait. Puppies. Cute or ugly?

295
00:19:12,270 --> 00:19:14,310
- Oh, so cute.     - Oh!

296
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:17,150
- Well? Ha, ha.     - You see?

297
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:19,860
But I'm still... I'm mad at you.

298
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:21,650
I know.

299
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:24,570
I'm mad at me too.

300
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:28,580
Well, um, do you want to get something to eat?

301
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:30,580
Because I'm kind of hungry.

302
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:32,540
Hey. Me too.

303
00:19:32,710 --> 00:19:35,960
All right, stop it. Now you're just doing it to freak me out.

304
00:19:42,050 --> 00:19:44,140
Aw, I missed you.

305
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:46,390
I missed you too.

306
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:52,270
Oh, I was so nervous about that letter.

307
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:57,270
But the way you owned up to everything...

308
00:19:57,440 --> 00:20:02,240
...it just showed me how much you've grown, you know?

309
00:20:04,450 --> 00:20:05,950
I suppose.

310
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:11,200
No. You have, Ross. You have. You should give yourself credit.

311
00:20:11,370 --> 00:20:14,710
I mean, my mom never thought this would work out.

312
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:18,710
Heh. She was all, "Once a cheater, always a cheater."

313
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:23,550
- Mm-hm.     - Oh.

314
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:26,640
I just wish we hadn't lost those four months.

315
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:32,430
But if time was what you needed just to gain a little perspective...

316
00:20:33,730 --> 00:20:36,480
We were on a break!

317
00:20:37,730 --> 00:20:39,940
- Coffeehouse?     - You bet.

318
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:44,530
And for the record, it took two people to break up this relationship.

319
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,820
Yeah, you and that girl from the copy place...

320
00:20:46,990 --> 00:20:49,580
...which yesterday you took full responsibility for.

321
00:20:49,740 --> 00:20:52,660
I didn't know what I was taking responsibility for, okay?

322
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:54,620
I didn't finish the whole letter.

323
00:20:54,790 --> 00:20:56,790
- What?     - I fell asleep.

324
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:59,170
You fell asleep?

325
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:02,920
Yeah, it was 5:30 in the morning.

326
00:21:03,090 --> 00:21:08,510
And you had rambled on for 18 pages.

327
00:21:09,390 --> 00:21:11,390
Front and back!

328
00:21:12,810 --> 00:21:14,430
Oh, oh, oh. And by the way.

329
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:18,190
"Y-O-U-apostrophe-R-E" means "you are."

330
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,110
"Y-O-U-R" means "your."

331
00:21:21,190 --> 00:21:24,320
I can't believe I even thought of getting back together with you.

332
00:21:24,490 --> 00:21:26,070
We are so over.

333
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:29,240
Fine by me!

334
00:21:30,530 --> 00:21:31,780
Oh, and hey, hey, hey.

335
00:21:31,950 --> 00:21:35,160
Those spelling tips will come in handy when you're at home on Saturday nights...

336
00:21:35,330 --> 00:21:36,790
...playing Scrabble with Monica.

337
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:39,000
- Hey.     - Sorry.

338
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:43,420
I just feel bad about all that sleep you're gonna miss, wishing you were with me.

339
00:21:43,590 --> 00:21:46,010
Oh, no, no. Don't you worry about me falling asleep.

340
00:21:46,470 --> 00:21:48,760
I still have your letter!

341
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:53,720
And hey, just so you know, it's not that common.

342
00:21:53,890 --> 00:21:57,810
It doesn't happen to every guy and it is a big deal!

343
00:21:58,730 --> 00:22:00,810
I knew it!

344
00:22:06,070 --> 00:22:07,280
Gin.

345
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:10,240
We were playing gin?

346
00:22:12,450 --> 00:22:15,240
You know, if we were a couple, we could play this game naked.

347
00:22:15,410 --> 00:22:18,080
- Ha, ha. Would you stop?     - Okay.

348
00:22:18,250 --> 00:22:19,750
All right.

349
00:22:20,330 --> 00:22:23,250
Okay, all right. I think you're great.

350
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:26,630
I think you're sweet and you're smart...

351
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:27,880
...and I love you.

352
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:32,680
But you will always be the guy who peed on me.

